# Katla-Çiz (Game 2)

## Rules (locked)
1. Vertical paper, **4 sections**: head, torso, legs, feet (top → bottom)
2. Players **2–4**; assign sections in order; with fewer than 4 players, wrap so one player may draw multiple sections
3. After finishing a section, **fold**; next drawer sees only a **peek strip** (bottom edge strokes of previous section)
4. Freehand: pointer events (mouse/touch/pen), pressure optional later
5. After last section → **reveal** full unfolded drawing
6. Local + online; no drawing bots unless explicitly requested

## Tech expectations
- Stroke model serializable (points + color + width) for Socket sync
- Authoritative turn index on server for online
- Canvas hit-testing only in active section; folded regions hidden/masked
- `window.render_game_to_text` hooks for harness when building playable prototype
